zcalloc: allocate with malloc(items * size)

Kind: game build change (no upstream release has it).

The reference zcalloc at 0x100092e0 is `mov eax,[esp+8]; imul eax,[esp+0xc];
push eax; call malloc (LIBCMT, 0x1001a7f7)`. Stock zlib 1.1.3 calls
calloc(items, size), as do 1.1.2 and 1.1.4 and Gilles Vollant's prebuilt
zlib113dll.zip static library (its _zcalloc pushes both arguments and calls
calloc). Building the stock zutil.c loads calloc.obj and moves 26164 bytes.
zlib 1.2.0 and later compute malloc(items * size) for 32-bit uInt, but no
release carries that with the 1.1.3 sources and version strings.

--- a/zutil.c
+++ b/zutil.c
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@
     unsigned size;
 {
     if (opaque) items += size - size; /* make compiler happy */
-    return (voidpf)calloc(items, size);
+    return (voidpf)malloc(items * size);
 }
 
 void  zcfree (opaque, ptr)
